mantle rm439
state ready
dialect plain
accent light broad
tier standard
written_for rm_soren_kelpstack
title the clerk of the drying line
fits stage=adult|old
prefers honesty=frank job=scholar
traits temper=even talk=plain warmth=reserved humour=dry honesty=frank piety=ordinary drive=steady
quirk judges_whether_rain_has_stopped_by_one_dry_line_on_the_sill
likes barley_soup riddles tidy_house warm_rain
dislikes stale_bread deep_mud
fears a_date_on_the_wrong_side an_undelivered_apology
hopes a_desk_where_the_rain_never_reaches_the_paper
topics work +0.5 weather +0.5 pastimes +0.3 food +0.2 gossip -0.3
styles comfort=practical gossip=plain refuse=direct tease=dry
marks oath saying
persona #self.first# rules a pencil line on the sill to settle arguments about the rain, tidies a desk by working off its contents, and insists that even a riddle must give an honest account of the question.

words
oath! = Rule my rain straight | Blot the forecast
saying! = Ask the sill for a date | A dry line settles a wet argument
dryline = my dry mark | the thin line under the lip
outside = the exposed end | the weather end
inkspot = an idle spot of ink | a small dark stop
pencilmark = a soft grey mark | a short ruling
ledgerback = the board at the back | my hard ledger cover
barleymeal = a bowl of barley | soup with a dozen grains to every spoon
spoontrack = a track left by a spoon | a little furrow in soup
wrongday = a date one day ahead | a number still waiting to happen
mudsplash = a comma of mud | a fat brown splash
breadstone = a very firm crust | a dry chunk of loaf
sillrag = my small drying cloth | an old strip of linen

any
opinion city for 1 : Anybody may observe Ridgemere's rain. The city is fairly democratic in its choice of observers.
opinion dole for 1 : A bowl issued now does more for a hungry body than an estimate issued tomorrow.
opinion road mixed 0 : I rate a road by whether the letter arrives fit to read.
opinion merchants mixed 0 : I'll defer to a merchant about the goods. I can add the figures without further assistance.
opinion houses mixed 0 : A House with a handsome heading still has to fit the business onto the page.
opinion festivals mixed 0 : The parade makes a superb procession. Its applications for space make a longer one.
opinion strangers for 1 : Anybody who knows which bit of path dries quickest is a welcome acquaintance on a wet day.

grown
line greet : There's a dry margin here quite wide enough for two.
line greet [pair.band=strangers] : A first visit. I'll leave the name column open.
line greet [here.time=dawn] : Morning, still subject to the weather's approval.
line greet [here.time=dusk|night] : Evening. The light gives me a legible outline of you.
line greet.return : Yes, welcome. I've dated the interruption favourably.
line greet.return [pair.band=friends|family] : Glad you're the one blotting out my view.
line greet.return [self.working=yes] : I can finish this stroke while you begin.
line greet.return [here.time=dusk|night] : At this hour the street's quiet enough to take dictation.
line kin.open [pair.kin!=no] : Family business can use ordinary paper.
line again.open : I have carried the unfinished portion over.
line hail [pair.band=friends] : Here, beyond reach of that dripping sill!
line farewell : Go before the road has a change of opinion.
line farewell.return : And arrive with your particulars still legible.
line react.news : Give the bare account a short space to dry.
line react.news.new : The original has only now crossed my desk.
line react.news.known : That appeared on an earlier page of the day.
line react.news.doubt : One of those figures seems to be doing unpaid overtime.
line react.news.sorrow [topic.kind=death|loss|theft|assault|arrest|crime] : Put the paper aside. That's a real hurt.
line react.news.glad [topic.kind=marriage|birth|apprentice|succession|work] : I'd happily clear a whole line for such a notice.
line ask.how : Has the day submitted a fair account of itself?
line answer.how : No worse than the estimate allowed for.
line thank : You removed a genuine difficulty. I value the distinction.
line deflect_thanks : No difficulty left worth putting in a note.
line sympathise : I can take the small errands off your list for a moment.
line reassure : It won't all need an answer on the present page.
line decline : I have another undertaking with a date rather inconveniently attached.
line accept_decline : A definite refusal is particularly easy to file.
line preclose : I'd best use the dry bit of afternoon before it expires.
line accept_preclose : May your walk come in under the estimate.

scene dry_marker
when topic=weather|smalltalk
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : #dryline.capitalize# has not been touched yet. | One end of a sill dries much earlier than the other.
b : You keep records of a windowsill? | Which one?
a : Naturally. The sill seems content enough with my clerking. | The sheltered end. A surprisingly contentious discovery in some rooms.

scene warm_fall
when topic=weather here.weather=rain
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Warm rain does little harm to anything except a timetable. | I can put my hand past #outside# and feel the exact warmth of this shower.
b : You enjoy being late? | Why bother?
a : I enjoy observing weather which shows no particular respect for my appointments. | My report can now be brief and accurate.

scene rain_stop
when topic=pastimes
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I like watching the last drop decide what to do. | A confident forecast of sunshine gets no lodging on my windowsill.
b : Has it much choice? | What forecast does?
a : Hang about or ruin a perfectly good announcement. | The pencil line when it starts to dry.

scene barley_count
when topic=food self.likes=barley_soup
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : #barleymeal.capitalize# is the only document I prefer with fewer blank spaces. | I measure hunger by the vanishing of #spoontrack#.
b : A very thick soup? | Does the soup run thin?
a : Thick enough for the spoon to find a few points worth considering. | No. I take the next spoonful too quickly to see.

scene honest_riddle
when topic=pastimes self.likes=riddles
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : What keeps a date after a wolf has broken it? | I favour riddles whose answers require no surprise uncles.
b : The disappointed caller? | Why an uncle?
a : An excellent answer. I was going to say the note of the appointment. | One can find a relative for almost any solution after the question is asked.

scene clean_room
when topic=home self.likes=tidy_house
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I clear a desk by working the stray bits off it. | A tidy room tells me which things are still lost.
b : Wouldn't a drawer save time? | Surely everything is in place.
a : Drawers merely give disorder a private address. | If everything were in place I should scarcely call anything lost.

scene bad_crust
when topic=food self.dislikes=stale_bread
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : #breadstone.capitalize# could keep my papers flat in a gale. | I keep dry bread out of the paper drawer.
b : Wouldn't it spoil the ink? | Who puts bread there?
a : No worse than it threatens to spoil my teeth. | A wolf seeking a use for it that doesn't involve chewing.

scene mud_papers
when topic=travel self.dislikes=deep_mud
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A wet boot tells you how deep a rut is once and too late. | I keep a folded paper inside the collar when the road looks doubtful.
b : Can a stick tell it sooner? | To report the mud?
a : Yes. A sensible arrangement between stick and boot. | To have one bit of the journey which doesn't weigh more on arriving.

scene proper_forms
when topic=work self.job=scholar
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Give a question its own row before losing it inside the answer. | I balance #ledgerback# on a dry knee.
b : Why separate them? | Working away from a desk?
a : An answer occasionally belongs to entirely different business. | I like a record even when a table is absent.

scene house_beside
when topic=home self.quarter=commons
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : The Commons can furnish six descriptions of one shower from six neighbouring doors. | I like watching a row of windows come open after rain.
b : Whose would you use? | For the light?
a : The one with a newly damp sill. | For the competition. Everybody wants to be right about the end.

scene clear_confidence
when topic=friends
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I can trust a friend to let a silence go unrecorded. | A pleasant companion may correct a sum without correcting my whole character.
b : Silence counts for something though? | A necessary skill?
a : Of course. It needn't be itemised. | Quite necessary if the company is to remain pleasant.

scene poor_paper
when topic=times world.times=hard|lean
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Dear paper invites better handwriting and smaller mistakes. | I put the next week's dates on scraps in hard times.
b : Smaller ones are cheaper? | And this week's?
a : Easier to squeeze in the margin beside a perfectly large bill. | Those I'm living through. They don't need a reminder quite so badly.

scene road_late
when topic=travel world.wagons=late
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Write the wagon down as late. Leave the column for an explanation blank. | I can account for my own waiting to the hour.
b : How long? | And the delay on the road?
a : Until a wheel or a witness turns up, preferably both. | The road hasn't signed a statement.

scene new_names
when topic=newcomer
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A new resident should have some say in how the name is written down. | For somebody new I would give directions in short lines.
b : Even an awkward spelling? | More paper?
a : An awkward spelling is no reason to confer an entirely new name. | Less chance of following a magnificent sentence straight to entirely the wrong door.

scene gossip_clause
when topic=gossip here.gossip=yes
does tell.gossip / react.self / assess
a : About #topic.subject# the wording was #topic.claim#. I have left out any conclusion. | #topic.subject.capitalize# #topic.claim#. A report with no signature in my possession.
b : Do you have one? | Would you repeat it?
a : I conclude that words were spoken. The rest would need a witness. | Only with that qualification sitting on the same line.

scene new_receipt
when topic=news world.news
does tell.news / react.self / assess
a : #world.news_from.capitalize# appears as the source beside #world.news#. | #world.news#. That gives the substance of the account from #world.news_from#.
b : How exact is that? | Is there an appendix?
a : As exact as the note. I could not legislate for the weather on its travels. | I sincerely hope my contribution hasn't made one necessary.

scene learn_letter
when topic=memories
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I learned my figures by counting things a rainstorm could carry away. | The first thing I wanted to write was a word proving I could write.
b : Like fallen fruit? | A signature?
a : Like my chalk marks. I had considerable practice making fresh ones. | A short word. I was ambitious within practical limits.

scene desk_dream
when topic=dreams
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : My ideal desk faces something which occasionally changes its mind. | I'd like my last sentence to make folding the letter a pleasure.
b : The square? | Aren't endings easy?
a : The sky. It provides amendments without requiring me to copy them. | Closing a letter, yes. Ending it before a second sheet is the art.

story dated_rain [topic=memories]
  : I dated a note one day ahead and left it where rain could reach it overnight.
  : The date dissolved at once. The note remained fairly readable.
  b : Did you put today's date back?
  : Waited overnight. First correction the weather and I ever made in agreement.

story paper_crust [topic=food|memories]
  : A dry crust once kept an open book at precisely the page I wanted.
  : I picked the book up by a corner without removing the bread.
  b : Where did it land?
  : In my soup. A satisfactory conclusion for all parties except the original reader of the book.

story three_roads [topic=travel|memories]
  : I wrote the names of three dry routes on a note for myself.
  : When I unfolded it the ink had run from one to the next.
  b : Any route left dry?
  : The crease, narrowly. I made a new map next morning and kept it inside my coat.

rule @rain_clip
when concept=bark here.weather=rain
does aside
cooldown 8h
say The very last drop has filed an extension.

rule @dry_grain
when concept=bark here.time=day
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Clear writing from here to the sill edge.

rule @pencil_wait
when concept=bark self.working=yes
does aside
cooldown 8h
say A short blank reserved for an actual observation.

rule @tidy_time
when concept=bark here.time=dusk
does aside
cooldown 8h
say One useless scrap has been promoted to a bookmark.

dlg resident.hub : State your case in whatever order the rain has left it.
dlg resident.hub [topic.meeting=known] : #topic.player#. I remember a previous entry under that face.
dlg resident.hub [here.time=night] : My ears can manage a question the lamp can no longer read.
dlg resident.hub [pair.disposition=hostile|wary] : Keep your present distance and your account pleasantly brief.
dlg resident.job [self.job=scholar] : #self.trade_words.capitalize#. I make uncertain matters fit legible rows.
dlg resident.job : I prefer work whose unfinished portions I can identify without a search party.
dlg resident.news [world.news] : My note reads #world.news#, filed under #world.news_from#.
dlg resident.gossip [here.gossip=yes] : An unsigned report runs like this: #topic.subject# #topic.claim#. Read the lack of a signature too.
dlg resident.bye : Choose a road that charges less for water.

graft resident.hub
choice Can a sill really settle a question? -> sill_question
node sill_question
say A suitably small question. I rule a short line where the roof just ceases to shelter the stone. Dry at both ends means I can carry my page out.
choice What about the way home? -> home_forecast
choice A useful bit of office equipment. -> hub
node home_forecast
say The sill has no jurisdiction over the way home. I generally keep that uncertainty folded under my coat.
choice I appreciate its limits. -> hub
choice I'll chance the return journey. -> bye
